<title>FRANCE: MATIF commodities volume jumps in January.</title>
<headline>MATIF commodities volume jumps in January.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of commodities futures and options traded on the French MATIF exchange in January jumped 132.1 percent from the previous month but fell 18.1 percent from January 1996, MATIF said in a statement.</p>
<p>Detailed figures were as follows.</p>
<p>		    Volume   Change	Change	 Open Positions</p>
<p>				on month    on year	 at end-month</p>
<p> All contracts  27,882    132.1	-18.1	     13,748</p>
<p> Total futures  27,782    133.2	-16.3	     13,698</p>
<p> of which</p>
<p> White sugar($)17,878    131.3	 -30.3		7,546</p>
<p> Potatoes	   259    -22.9	 -85.4		  580</p>
<p> Rapeseed	 8,545    178.2	  48.4		4,562</p>
<p> Wheat	    1,100     42.1	   NA		 1,010</p>
<p> Sugar options    100	0.0	   NA		    50</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
